#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115050 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6b41a05-7b11-52b8-a407-af505dffaf10" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Data Set Using the Definition"}] :question/id #uuid "e148a574-9aa3-57f1-a186-4fbd543db3e7" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-7638" :question/problem "What is the variance of the following data set?\n$5, \\: 13, \\: 6, \\: 8, \\: 3$" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points $x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n$, then the variance of the data set is given by\n\n$$\n\\sigma^2 = \\dfrac{1}{n} \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^n (x_i - \\overline{x})^2\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{1}{n} \\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^n x_i\n$$\n\nis the mean of the data set.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the mean. There are $n=5$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^(―) &= \\frac{1}{n}∑_(i = 1)^(n)x_{i} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5} \\cdot (5 + 13 + 6 + 8 + 3) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5} \\cdot 35 \\\\\n&= 7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nσ^{2} &= \\frac{1}{n}∑_(i = 1)^(n)(x_{i} - x^(―))^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5}[(5 - 7)^{2} + (13 - 7)^{2} + (6 - 7)^{2} + (8 - 7)^{2} + (3 - 7)^{2}] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5}[4 + 36 + 1 + 1 + 16] \\\\\n&= \\frac{58}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115051 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0040fc1-2134-5eaa-a3e8-6c7a457f75f5" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Data Set Using the Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "83414114-1b1d-5500-9a38-648a90d0244c" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-7639" :question/problem "What is the variance of the following data set?\n$4, \\: 5, \\: 4, \\: 7, \\: 8, \\: 11, \\: 3$" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points $x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n$, then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n\\sigma^2 = \\overline{x^2} - (\\overline{x})^2\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overline{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overline{x^2}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overline{x}$. There are $n=7$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^(―) &= \\frac{1}{n}∑_(i = 1)^(n)x_{i} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{7} \\cdot (4 + 5 + 4 + 7 + 8 + 11 + 3) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{7} \\cdot 42 \\\\\n&= 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overline{x^2}$. Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2}^(―) &= \\frac{1}{n}∑_(i = 1)^(n)x_{i}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{7} \\cdot (4^{2} + 5^{2} + 4^{2} + 7^{2} + 8^{2} + 11^{2} + 3^{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{7} \\cdot (16 + 25 + 16 + 49 + 64 + 121 + 9) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{7} \\cdot 300 \\\\\n&= \\frac{300}{7}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nσ^{2} &= x^{2}^(―) - (x^(―))^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{300}{7} - (6)^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{300}{7} - 36 \\\\\n&= \\frac{300 - 252}{7} \\\\\n&= \\frac{48}{7}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115052 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a72dae6-2bbf-5e59-b71d-8ee57f589753" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Standard Deviation of a Data Set"}] :question/id #uuid "a1d37026-f331-5e80-8640-00289af07606" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-7640" :question/problem "What is the standard deviation of the following data set?\n$7, \\: 5, \\: 0, \\: 2, \\: 1, \\: 3$" :question/worked-solution "The standard deviation of a data set $x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n$ is the square root of the variance:\n\n$$\n\\sigma = \\sqrt{\\sigma^2} = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{1}{n} \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^n (x_i - \\overline{x})^2} = \\sqrt{\\,\\,\\, \\vphantom{\\sum\\limits_{i=1}^n} \\overline{x^2} - \\left(\\overline{x} \\right)^2}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overline{x}$. There are $n=6$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^(―) &= \\frac{1}{n}∑_(i = 1)^(n)x_{i} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6} \\cdot (7 + 5 + 0 + 2 + 1 + 3) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6} \\cdot 18 \\\\\n&= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overline{x^2}$. Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2}^(―) &= \\frac{1}{n}∑_(i = 1)^(n)x_{i}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6} \\cdot (7^{2} + 5^{2} + 0^{2} + 2^{2} + 1^{2} + 3^{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6} \\cdot (49 + 25 + 0 + 4 + 1 + 9) \\\\\n&= \\frac{88}{6} \\\\\n&= \\frac{44}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nσ^{2} &= x^{2}^(―) - (x^(―))^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{44}{3} - (3)^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{44}{3} - 9 \\\\\n&= \\frac{44 - 27}{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{17}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the standard deviation is\n\n$$\n\\sigma = \\sqrt{\\sigma^2} = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{17}{3}}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115053 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eab4249-544e-56c6-81c0-e6db84033701" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance Given the Number, Sum, and Sum of Squares of the Data Points"}] :question/id #uuid "234b1f04-e423-5d6f-8084-15b55d0632ca" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-7641" :question/problem "Compute the variance $\\sigma^2$ of a data set $x_i$ consisting of $8$ data points, where\n\n$\\sum_{i=1}^{8} x_i = 40, \\qquad \\sum_{i=1}^{8} x_i^2 = 320$." :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points $x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n$, then the variance of the data set is given by\n\n$$\n\\sigma^2 = \\overline{x^2} - (\\overline{x})^2\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overline{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overline{x^2}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overline{x}$. There are $n=8$ points in our data set, and we know that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{8} x_i = 40\n$$\n\nso we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^(―) &= \\frac{1}{n}∑_(i = 1)^(n)x_{i} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{8}∑_(i = 1)^(8)x_{i} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{8} \\cdot 40 \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overline{x^2}$. We know that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{8} x_i^2 = 320\n$$\n\nso we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2}^(―) &= \\frac{1}{n}∑_(i = 1)^(n)x_{i}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{8}∑_(i = 1)^(8)x_{i}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{8} \\cdot 320 \\\\\n&= 40\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nσ^{2} &= x^{2}^(―) - (x^(―))^{2} \\\\\n&= 40 - (5)^{2} \\\\\n&= 40 - 25 \\\\\n&= 15\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245737 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a72dae6-2bbf-5e59-b71d-8ee57f589753" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Standard Deviation of a Data Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d267a77-677c-5074-a988-8dba8e441b0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245739} {:answer/id #uuid "1abb5f15-8c52-5b2c-b7ee-3c17ad5462dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245740} {:answer/id #uuid "62b96511-4b8c-53be-b569-3be44b7da380" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{31}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245741} {:answer/id #uuid "e0a6a367-e882-5e36-8d66-792cb2b30b69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{46}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245742} {:answer/id #uuid "37b8b58c-28d6-5f47-9bb5-479d139a3047" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0a6a367-e882-5e36-8d66-792cb2b30b69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{46}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245742} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad856cf7-9175-504f-852b-e2f333b6ba6c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245738}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "575c9e3c-af66-5729-a91e-0c9de5b64e10" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-166585" :question/problem "What is the standard deviation of the following data set?\n\n$$\n7,\\,4,\\,11,\\,2,\\,6\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The standard deviation of a data set ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is the square root of the variance:\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\,\\,\\,\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=5$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (7+4+11+2+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 30 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot ({7}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{11}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{6}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (49+16+121+4+36) \\\\  & =\\frac{226}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{226}{5}-{(6)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{226}{5}-36 \\\\  & =\\frac{226-180}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{46}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the standard deviation is\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{46}{5}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245744 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6b41a05-7b11-52b8-a407-af505dffaf10" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Data Set Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2048d606-0888-5c13-bb07-acf4b1bb54fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{43}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245746} {:answer/id #uuid "b88a22f6-1ed9-5c79-9092-1fd04da68a94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{43}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245747}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b88a22f6-1ed9-5c79-9092-1fd04da68a94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{43}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245747} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d6fa9e8-9866-5d83-8c96-da376ae8a15f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245745}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d2a3b06a-d69e-536d-b805-8142d5ea37d0" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-246716" :question/problem "Compute the variance ${\\sigma }^{2}$ of the following data set:\n\n$$\n10,\\,23,\\,17,\\,18\n$$\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance of the data set is given by \n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ is the mean of the data set.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the mean. There are $n=4$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (10+23+17+18) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 68 \\\\  & =17.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(10-17)^{2}+(23-17)^{2}+(17-17)^{2}+(18-17)^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[49+36+0+1] \\\\  & =\\frac{86}{4} \\\\  & =21.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245748 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0040fc1-2134-5eaa-a3e8-6c7a457f75f5" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Data Set Using the Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5175476a-fa2a-574d-8778-e574709d52cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{74}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245750} {:answer/id #uuid "9863e07b-2506-50ab-a86b-7acfbcddaba7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{37}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245751}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9863e07b-2506-50ab-a86b-7acfbcddaba7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{37}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245751} :answer-field/id #uuid "d71e666a-672d-51fa-8c3d-eb2e0b29bc90" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245749}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0d4f682c-c60d-5829-8c4d-e7ed9d401f55" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-246721" :question/problem "What is the variance of the following data set?\n\n$$\n12,\\,15,\\,15,\\,17,\\,21,\\,22\n$$\n\nDo not round your answer.\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=6$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (12+15+15+17+21+22) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 102 \\\\  & =17.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot ({12}^{2}+{15}^{2}+{15}^{2}+{17}^{2}+{21}^{2}+{22}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (144+225+225+289+441+484) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 1808 \\\\  & =\\frac{1808}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{904}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{904}{3}-{(17)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{904}{3}-289 \\\\  & =\\frac{904-867}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{37}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115489 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a72dae6-2bbf-5e59-b71d-8ee57f589753" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Standard Deviation of a Data Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6109e8da-0ddf-5915-8253-a0fb57f138a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{716/25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6109e8da-0ddf-5915-8253-a0fb57f138a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{716/25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232799} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b3b2d4f-dd88-551d-938f-f7afeff7970e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112334}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5710fea8-dfda-5618-84dc-c9d9011e12ae" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-246726" :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nCompute the standard deviation $σ$ of the following data set:\n$-9,-7, 1, 3, 4$\n\nDo not round your answer.\n\n$σ =$\n{{field-1}}\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"why-we-use-the-squared-difference\"></a>" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The standard deviation of a data set ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is the square root of the variance:\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\,\\,\\,\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=5$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (-9-7+1+3+4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot [(-9)^{2}+(-7)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot [81+49+1+9+16] \\\\  & =\\frac{156}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{156}{5}-{(-\\frac{8}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{156}{5}-\\frac{64}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{780-64}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{716}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the standard deviation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sigma  & =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{716}{25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{179}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245752 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6b41a05-7b11-52b8-a407-af505dffaf10" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Data Set Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f26b5147-ea3f-5baa-88a7-47a9b0cba9eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f26b5147-ea3f-5baa-88a7-47a9b0cba9eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245754} :answer-field/id #uuid "69ecaea7-9779-515a-acc2-c3ebff64699e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245753}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bbd753fe-03e2-53a5-a2b0-e6fa1fba36c6" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-263258" :question/problem "Compute the variance ${\\sigma }^{2}$ of the following data set:\n\n$$\n14,\\,21,\\,13,\\,16\n$$\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance of the data set is given by \n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ is the mean of the data set.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the mean. There are $n=4$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (14+21+13+16) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 64 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(14-16)^{2}+(21-16)^{2}+(13-16)^{2}+(16-16)^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[4+25+9+0] \\\\  & =\\frac{38}{4} \\\\  & =9.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245755 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6b41a05-7b11-52b8-a407-af505dffaf10" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Data Set Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34ab0069-2ae3-52dd-81ec-da5f8966e2db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{65}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34ab0069-2ae3-52dd-81ec-da5f8966e2db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{65}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245757} :answer-field/id #uuid "31c0de7c-d4c0-50e9-a691-f4cd8a9872cb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245756}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c83c3ac2-cbf3-5dd1-9b5c-3ade2eb7f446" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-263297" :question/problem "Compute the variance ${\\sigma }^{2}$ of the following data set:\n\n$$\n1,\\,-6,\\,-1,\\,3,\\,-11,\\,-4\n$$\n\nDo not round your answer.\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance of the data set is given by \n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ is the mean of the data set.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the mean. There are $n=6$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (1-6-1+3-11-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-18) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(1-(-3))^{2}+(-6-(-3))^{2}+(-1-(-3))^{2}+(3-(-3))^{2}+(-11-(-3))^{2}+(-4-(-3))^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[16+9+4+36+64+1] \\\\  & =\\frac{130}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{65}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245758 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eab4249-544e-56c6-81c0-e6db84033701" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance Given the Number, Sum, and Sum of Squares of the Data Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ffd3ed0-e971-5edb-8457-712a850039d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245760}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ffd3ed0-e971-5edb-8457-712a850039d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245760} :answer-field/id #uuid "b13fe170-c190-5efc-a199-be13be238598" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245759}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c6ac209e-57e0-5a4e-a63e-ea34749b87d1" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-263301" :question/problem "Compute the variance ${\\sigma }^{2}$ of a data set ${x}_{i}$ consisting of $8$ data points, where\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}=64,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}^{2}=768.\n$$\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=8$ points in our data set, and we know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}=64,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot (64) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ We know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}^{2}=768,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot 768 \\\\  & =96.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =96-{(8)}^{2} \\\\  & =96-64 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245761 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eab4249-544e-56c6-81c0-e6db84033701" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance Given the Number, Sum, and Sum of Squares of the Data Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df0be136-e51e-5720-b004-f890a3a69cf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245763} {:answer/id #uuid "fd31c25e-af56-5f49-a037-0cd3da7f69a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245764}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df0be136-e51e-5720-b004-f890a3a69cf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245763} :answer-field/id #uuid "17c4ca46-cb0e-59e0-b93f-0a4c160d669b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245762}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d71b5626-730b-55f2-b59e-5134ae2d2058" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-263335" :question/problem "Compute the variance ${\\sigma }^{2}$ of a data set ${x}_{i}$ consisting of $8$ data points, where\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}=104,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}^{2}=1448.\n$$\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=8$ points in our data set, and we know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}=104,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot (104) \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ We know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}^{2}=1448,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot 1448 \\\\  & =181.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =181-{(13)}^{2} \\\\  & =181-169 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245765 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eab4249-544e-56c6-81c0-e6db84033701" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance Given the Number, Sum, and Sum of Squares of the Data Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d0fb512-2e42-5d4c-977e-5208c4a16664" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245767} {:answer/id #uuid "c3accf2a-2c1b-5ca4-bd51-a0316c96b6e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3accf2a-2c1b-5ca4-bd51-a0316c96b6e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245768} :answer-field/id #uuid "f87ca57c-c616-5471-add2-945e1cf9b8dd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245766}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ea453a50-9c54-592d-912a-295192095ae6" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-263343" :question/problem "Compute the variance ${\\sigma }^{2}$ of a data set ${x}_{i}$ consisting of $8$ data points, where\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}=-112,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}^{2}=1736.\n$$\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=8$ points in our data set, and we know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}=-112,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot (-112) \\\\  & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ We know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}^{2}=1736,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot 1736 \\\\  & =217.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =217-{(-14)}^{2} \\\\  & =217-196 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245769 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0040fc1-2134-5eaa-a3e8-6c7a457f75f5" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Data Set Using the Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8128b79-a5f2-50f7-80f3-eab191508e97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{232}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245771} {:answer/id #uuid "886a6db8-789b-5634-a15c-b992de4760ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{340}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8128b79-a5f2-50f7-80f3-eab191508e97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{232}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245771} :answer-field/id #uuid "32810a8b-a236-5c4b-a5b3-606310c382f4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245770}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c07b3c70-2064-5066-bec2-89d0b2cf1e30" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-263435" :question/problem "What is the variance of the following data set?\n\n$$\n-12,\\,-14,\\,-7,\\,11,\\,-15,\\,5,\\,0,\\,-8,\\,-14\n$$\n\nDo not round your answer.\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=9$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot (-12-14-7+11-15+5+0-8-14) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot (-54) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot ((-12)^{2}+(-14)^{2}+(-7)^{2}+{11}^{2}+(-15)^{2}+{5}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-8)^{2}+(-14)^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot (144+196+49+121+225+25+0+64+196) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot 1020 \\\\  & =\\frac{1020}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{340}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{340}{3}-{(-6)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{340}{3}-36 \\\\  & =\\frac{340-108}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{232}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245773 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0040fc1-2134-5eaa-a3e8-6c7a457f75f5" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Data Set Using the Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1d26837-310e-58f0-a029-890e34a7b8af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{415}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1d26837-310e-58f0-a029-890e34a7b8af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{415}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245775} :answer-field/id #uuid "47fdbeaf-5c35-5b80-80f9-04308a3c6ea9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245774}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "60280ea3-ddd0-5a95-9e4a-e5f69d56d7f4" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-263447" :question/problem "What is the variance of the following data set?\n\n$$\n-12,\\,1,\\,-7,\\,9,\\,7,\\,13,\\,-12,\\,-15\n$$\n\nDo not round your answer.\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=8$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot (-12+1-7+9+7+13-12-15) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot (-16) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot ((-12)^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-7)^{2}+{9}^{2}+{7}^{2}+{13}^{2}+(-12)^{2}+(-15)^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot (144+1+49+81+49+169+144+225) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot 862 \\\\  & =\\frac{862}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{431}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{431}{4}-{(-2)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{431}{4}-4 \\\\  & =\\frac{431-16}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{415}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245776 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eab4249-544e-56c6-81c0-e6db84033701" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance Given the Number, Sum, and Sum of Squares of the Data Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a057ea2-aeac-5e64-bc9f-9dfc22b4b1c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245778} {:answer/id #uuid "c20c13d6-924e-5e4e-bede-b09ec5d56fe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245779} {:answer/id #uuid "04333eeb-be88-5ac4-ad88-f0772250a59b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245780} {:answer/id #uuid "de1cd017-4414-5328-99e7-7a79015861be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245781} {:answer/id #uuid "9e5ef32c-f74f-5ae7-a413-9df0612f59cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245782}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e5ef32c-f74f-5ae7-a413-9df0612f59cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245782} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ba88001-261a-508d-b1d7-ee26d2fbef9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245777}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "97b5a09c-ba97-5deb-97d8-4bd8abb87bfa" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-87253" :question/problem "Compute the variance ${\\sigma }^{2}$ of a data set ${x}_{i}$ consisting of $15$ data points, where \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{x}_{i}=-30,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{x}_{i}^{2}=120.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=15$ points in our data set, and we know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{x}_{i}=-30,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15}\\cdot (-30) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ We know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{x}_{i}^{2}=120,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15}\\cdot 120 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =8-{(-2)}^{2} \\\\  & =8-4 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245783 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6b41a05-7b11-52b8-a407-af505dffaf10" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Data Set Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7512ef5-0eeb-585c-b07a-079ddbe0d77f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{88}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245785} {:answer/id #uuid "9fd36aab-53a6-5e41-a336-656695904932" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245786} {:answer/id #uuid "f4e84b46-9162-50e2-9572-94c6732c0ba3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245787} {:answer/id #uuid "2caf0726-cc42-5498-a770-2e8181eef8c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{175}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245788} {:answer/id #uuid "050ecf80-caa5-5a1e-98b3-1fe6e027472d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{79}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7512ef5-0eeb-585c-b07a-079ddbe0d77f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{88}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245785} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c264da9-64ee-541a-a69f-ac10499f855b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245784}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "43a803fe-7810-57d7-ba47-44721a266a52" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-87461" :question/problem "What is the variance of the following data set?\n\n$$\n3,\\,1,\\,15,\\,3,\\,2,\\,12\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance of the data set is given by \n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ is the mean of the data set.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the mean. There are $n=6$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (3+1+15+3+2+12) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 36 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(3-6)^{2}+(1-6)^{2}+(15-6)^{2}+(3-6)^{2}+(2-6)^{2}+(12-6)^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[9+25+81+9+16+36] \\\\  & =\\frac{176}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{88}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186245790 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6b41a05-7b11-52b8-a407-af505dffaf10" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Data Set Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "268c2c25-f576-5d6a-bc83-d834a74b0e34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245792} {:answer/id #uuid "27ee5811-0457-5d22-8e76-027d72a97d72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value 